        "text": "*[Bug 19117] New: strptime() parses shortest prefix of localised month name*\n<https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=19117>\n\n            Bug ID: 19117\n           Summary: strptime() parses shortest prefix of localised month\n                    name\n           Product: R\n           Version: R 4.6.x\n          Hardware: Other\n                OS: All\n            Status: NEW\n          Severity: normal\n          Priority: P5\n         Component: Low-level\n          Assignee: <mailto:R-core@R-project.org|R-core@R-project.org>\n          Reporter: <mailto:ikrylov@disroot.org|ikrylov@disroot.org>\n\nIn some locales, `strptime()` will misunderstand month names if some of them\nare prefixes of others:\n\n```\n# sudo apt install locales-all,\n#  or add \"vi_VN UTF-8\" to \/etc\/locale.gen and run locale-gen\nSys.setlocale(\"LC_TIME\", \"vi_VN\")\nd &lt;- as.Date('2000-11-01')\nf &lt;- '%Y %d %b'\nd |&gt; strftime(f) |&gt; strptime(f)\n# [1] \"2000-01-01 UTC\"\n```\n\nThis happens because in the vi_VN locale, month names are formatted as \"Tháng\n1\" ... \"Tháng 12\" (`%B`) or \"Thg 1\" ... \"Thg 12\" (`%b`) and R's own internal\n`strptime()` [parses them\nas](<https:\/\/svn.r-project.org\/browse\/R\/trunk\/src\/main\/Rstrptime.h?op=blame&amp;rev=83234#l297>):\n\n```\nif (w_match_string (w_weekday_name[cnt], rp)) break;\n\/\/ ...\nif (w_match_string (w_ab_weekday_name[cnt], rp)) break;\n```\n\n...i.e., as soon as R sees \"Thg 1\", the match is successful. This leads to\nproblems with the `%b` format in the following locales:\n\n* bo_CN\n* bo_IN\n* dz_BT\n* km_KH\n* tok\n* shn_MM (where July (\"လၼသပး\") is a prefix of November (\"လၼသပးသင\"))\n* vi_VN",
