        "text": "*[Bug 19118] New: byte compiler: missing protect in switch handler*\n<https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=19118>\n\n            Bug ID: 19118\n           Summary: byte compiler: missing protect in switch handler\n           Product: R\n           Version: R-devel (trunk)\n          Hardware: Other\n                OS: Other\n            Status: NEW\n          Severity: normal\n          Priority: P5\n         Component: Low-level\n          Assignee: <mailto:R-core@R-project.org|R-core@R-project.org>\n          Reporter: <mailto:kevinushey@gmail.com|kevinushey@gmail.com>\n\nTo reproduce:\n\n```\noptions(warn = -1)                      # only to keep the transcript short\nmkf &lt;- function() factor(\"b\", levels = c(\"a\", \"b\"))\ng &lt;- compiler::cmpfun(function() switch(mkf(), a = \"GOT_A\", b = \"GOT_B\"))\ngctorture(TRUE)\nfor (k in 1:4) cat(\"call\", k, \"-&gt;\", format(g()), \"\\n\")\ngctorture(FALSE)\n```\n\nIn this case, I see:\n\n```\ncall 1 -&gt; NULL\ncall 2 -&gt; NULL\ncall 3 -&gt; NULL\ncall 4 -&gt; NULL\n```\n\nrather than the expected `GOT_B` result.",
